      "question": "We filtered the oil on Transformer 1 at site MAIN in early January, and I need a clean pre-filtration baseline to compare against. Pull the hydrogen, methane, ethylene, acetylene and co readings for every oil sample taken in the two months before 2024-01-15T00:00:00.000000. Give me the min, max and mean of each gas over that pre-January period, and the average daily rise in ppm/day for hydrogen and acetylene. Then tell me by what percentage each gas is lower in the latest sample than in that baseline, so I can judge how much the filtration is masking the fault gases.",
